## What the close found on the way

**`.gitattributes` would have corrupted the two PNG renders.** Staging them produced
`warning: CRLF will be replaced by LF` — the blanket `* text eol=lf` rule reaching binary
content, which is precisely what `ECR-D-015` recorded for the 24 binary deliverables. That file's
own comment says *"Re-run that check before adding any"*. It was re-run, it fired, and
`portfolio/renders/** -text` is the answer. Both PNGs now round-trip byte-identically through the
index; all 61 existing binary deliverables were re-checked and still do.

**DC-1 cannot pin a binary at all.** Pinning the renders in `R-031` raised `UnicodeDecodeError` —
DC-1 decodes UTF-8 before hashing. That is the construction refusing rather than guessing, and it
is the same reason `cad/DELIVERABLES.md` registers the PDF and STL deliverables by raw SHA-256
over octets. The renders are therefore unpinned and regenerable; the script that produces them is
pinned, and it is byte-deterministic across re-runs.

